From 828ad8b8c6b7f2dd1b7a157c2edeb4cd26955a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ygecesefa <ygecesefa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:04:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Decrypt /data: KeyMint, qseecomd and gatekeeper from the
 tablet's vendor

LineageOS 22 encrypts /data with FBE v2, hardware-wrapped keys and
metadata encryption (dm-default-key). TWRP V2 had none of the userspace
for it and failed with 'Failed to mount /data (Invalid argument)'; the
kernel side (DM_DEFAULT_KEY, inline crypto, HWKM, smcinvoke) is there.

- system/bin: qseecomd, android.hardware.security.keymint-service-qti,
  android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0-service; vendor/lib64: their vendor
  dependencies (readelf closure), all from this tablet's /vendor
  (X710XXU4BXHB), so they match its TrustZone apps.
- vendor/etc/vintf: the tablet's own manifest (the tree carried a
  Galaxy Z Fold 5 one) plus the KeyMint fragment.
- init.recovery.keymint.rc: start KeyMint once qseecomd has registered
  its listeners; twrp-common does qseecomd and gatekeeper.
- BoardConfig: TWRP FBE + metadata decryption, Qualcomm FBE, fscrypt v2;
  device.mk: qcom_decrypt(_fbe); twrp.dependencies: twrp-common.
- system.prop: keystore/gatekeeper = mdfpp, dm-default-key v2.
